            <ArticleTitle>[Fever and right upper abdominal pain in a 26-year-old returning from travel abroad].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1475-6, 1478-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00108-014-3545-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Persistent fever and unspecific general symptoms need a complete and detailed medical history and search for infection. We report on a case of amebiasis with liver abscesses of a 26-year-old man. He had stayed several weeks in India and South America. After being free of complaints for 4 months, unspecific general symptoms and fever appeared. Due to proven liver abscesses, a combination treatment was given. Within 12 days, he was free of symptoms and could be discharged.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
